    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **23 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` assignment following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**What the feature does:** on owner creation, sets `membershipNumber` to `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where YY is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AssignMembershipNumber`** (new function) \u2014 a single-method `service(@Val Owner owner)` step that reads the already-assigned `customerCode` and `registrationDate` off the owner and sets the derived membership number. Zero-pads the year via `%02d`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline after `assignNamesakeCount` and before `save` (so both `customerCode` and the defaulted `registrationDate` are present), carrying the same `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `membership_number VARCHAR(30)` to all four dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). Tests run under `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it by name automatically (making it appear in both the POST response and GET fetch used by the test).\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests` passes and no existing tests regressed.",
